# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Packaging / build
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Test & coverage artefacts
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Property-testing database. Hypothesis drops a self-ignoring `.gitignore` into
# each directory it creates, but that file is its to delete and re-create, and
# it invites deletion in its own comment. The rule belongs here, where this
# repository states its own intent. No leading slash, so it matches at every
# level: the workspace root, each member, and any mutants/ copy.
.hypothesis/

# Type checker / linter caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json

# Mutation testing. `mutmut run` copies the whole tree into mutants/ and
# rewrites the sources there; nothing in it is authored.
mutants/
mutants.sqlite

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# SDD scratch
.superpowers/

# Wayfinder maps and issue tracker: live working state, not history. A captured
# behaviour-lock reference lands here too (.scratch/lock/) and stays ignored: it
# is a fact about one machine's kernel build, not about this repository -- ADR-0011.
.scratch/

# Internal working records. These drift: a plan describes one session's intent,
# the backlog tracks what is not yet decided, and a technical specification is
# written ahead of the code and amended behind it. The decisions that survived
# are in docs/adr/, which is the authority; docs/FOUNDATION.md and
# docs/GLOSSARY.md carry the model and the vocabulary. Published code cites
# those and never one of these.
docs/BACKLOG.md
docs/specs/
docs/plans/

# Session docs that might go stale
docs/superpowers/

# Agent worktrees (native harness-managed)
.claude/worktrees/

# Agent worktrees (manual fallback)
.worktrees/

# Proprietary docs that can be found outside this repository
docs/parts/*.pdf
docs/iso/
